---
title: Yay Basics
order: 1
description: yay -S, -Ss, -Si, -Sua, install AUR packages
tags: [yay, aur, install, search, update]
---

Basic yay usage mirrors pacman syntax. yay searches both official repos
and the AUR simultaneously.

@code bash
# ---- installing packages ----

yay -S package                            # install (AUR or official)
yay -S package1 package2                  # install multiple
yay package                               # interactive search + install
yay                                       # equivalent to yay -Syu (full upgrade)

@text
When installing an AUR package, yay will:
1. Download the PKGBUILD from the AUR
2. Show you the PKGBUILD for review (first install or changes)
3. Resolve and install dependencies
4. Build the package with makepkg
5. Install the built package with pacman

@code bash
# ---- searching ----

yay -Ss search-term                       # search AUR + repos
yay -Ss --aur search-term                # AUR only
yay -Ss --repo search-term              # repos only

yay -Si package                           # info from repos or AUR
yay -Si --aur package                    # AUR info only

# interactive search
yay search-term                           # list matches, select by number

@code bash
# ---- upgrading ----

yay -Syu                                  # upgrade everything (repos + AUR)
yay -Sua                                  # upgrade AUR packages only
yay -Syu --devel                          # also check -git/-svn packages

# check for updates without installing
yay -Qu                                   # all updates available
yay -Qua                                  # AUR updates only

# check what would be upgraded
checkupdates                              # official repos
yay -Qua                                  # AUR

@code bash
# ---- querying ----

yay -Qm                                   # list foreign packages (AUR/manual)
yay -Qmq                                  # names only
yay -Qi package                           # package info (same as pacman)
yay -Ql package                           # list files (same as pacman)

@code bash
# ---- removing ----

# removal is the same as pacman (yay passes through)
yay -R package                            # remove
yay -Rs package                           # remove + unneeded deps
yay -Rns package                          # remove + deps + configs

@code bash
# ---- useful options ----

yay -S package --noconfirm                # skip all prompts
yay -S package --needed                   # skip if already installed
yay -S package --mflags "--nocheck"       # skip check() in PKGBUILD
yay -S package --rebuild                  # force rebuild
yay -S package --redownload               # force re-download PKGBUILD

# build in a clean chroot (avoids host pollution)
yay -S package --sudoloop                 # keep sudo alive during long builds

@text
First-time setup: yay itself is installed from the AUR.

@code bash
# install yay
pacman -S --needed git base-devel
git clone https://aur.archlinux.org/yay.git
cd yay
makepkg -si
cd .. && rm -rf yay

# or use yay-bin (pre-built binary, faster)
git clone https://aur.archlinux.org/yay-bin.git
cd yay-bin
makepkg -si
cd .. && rm -rf yay-bin
